WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.12 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Monitoring and reviewing risk

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Early risks change fast: review them often and watch for warning signs from launch.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
Monitoring risk means checking regularly whether your risks are growing, shrinking or new. In the early days risks change quickly, so reviews need to be frequent and linked to your work.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
Three monitoring habits

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:38.981
Regular review: High risks monthly, others quarterly, and the whole register once or twice a year. For example: Each month the two founders spend ten minutes on their four high risks.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:49.941
Early warning signs: Indicators that a risk is growing, watched before it happens. For example: Cash below two months of runway, or fewer than four referrals for the next intake.

7
00:00:49.941 --> 00:01:02.470
Learning from issues: When a risk happens, respond, then ask what the register missed. For example: After a café paid late, the bakery adds a new risk about wholesale payment terms.

8
00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:03.470
Why keep watching

9
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.774
1. Early risks change fast; an old register gives false comfort.

10
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:14.448
2. Warning signs give you time to act before harm is done.

11
00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:20.381
3. Each review turns experience into learning while you build.

12
00:01:20.781 --> 00:01:21.381
Where it connects

13
00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:26.685
1. The meeting where each objective, partner or task is managed.

14
00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:31.248
2. Your cash flow triggers and your management accounts.

15
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:37.922
3. Your issue log from Module 5, when a risk becomes real.

16
00:01:38.322 --> 00:01:38.922
What to avoid

17
00:01:38.922 --> 00:01:44.226
Writing the register once and never looking at it again.

18
00:01:44.226 --> 00:01:48.789
Discussing risks apart from the work they threaten.

19
00:01:48.789 --> 00:01:54.352
Responding to an issue without updating the register.

20
00:01:54.952 --> 00:01:56.752
You set your risk review routine and early warning indicators.

21
00:01:56.752 --> 00:02:00.752
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:02.252 --> 00:02:05.352
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
